This happens to me on Windows 10 with libtorch-win-shared-with-deps-1.12.1+cu116

Project compiled with VS 2019 :

		torch::Tensor t1=torch::rand({2,2});
		torch::Tensor t2=torch::rand({2,2});
		std::cout << "t1 = " << t1 << "\n";
		std::cout << "t2 = " << t2 << "\n";
		std::cout << torch::cat({t1,t2},1) << std::endl;
		
And crashes in the torch::cat() function.

Do we have a way to pick up a fix and is there a unit test that is implemented for torch::cat or other APIs on Windows, that I can monitor to check with release would have the fix?
